What Is the Grid-Forming Inverter Control Software Market?
Grid-forming inverter control software enables inverter-based energy resources to establish and regulate voltage and frequency references within electricity networks. It supports grid stability as renewable energy and battery storage installations increase, helping power systems respond to disturbances and operate reliably with a growing share of inverter-based generation.

Key Market Drivers
Increasing Demand for Grid Stability and Reliability
The expansion of renewable energy and battery storage is increasing the need for advanced grid control capabilities. Grid-forming technology helps inverter-based resources contribute to voltage and frequency stability, creating demand for specialised software, controller configuration and commissioning services.

Growing Battery Storage Deployment
Utility-scale battery projects are increasingly incorporating advanced inverter functions to support grid services beyond conventional energy storage. As developers and utilities adopt these systems, demand is rising for software that can meet grid connection requirements and demonstrate stable performance.

