Market Challenges
Grid-forming software must operate reliably across different network conditions, inverter architectures and grid requirements. Interoperability testing, technical validation and the need for specialised engineering expertise can increase project complexity and extend deployment timelines.

Market Restraints
Bundling software with inverter hardware can make it difficult to establish separate software pricing and revenue streams. Lengthy qualification procedures, converter current limitations and shortages of experienced control engineers may also slow market expansion.

